/* The Related strip (STRUCTURE_AUDIT.md section D, 22 November 2026): the pure core (src/js/2z-related-core.js), the drawing and the page foot (src/js/6zzh-related.js) and the pages that call it.
   The bundle is rebuilt here the way the build does it (the sources in sorted order, one scope) against the REAL data: the Library, the passage index, the calendars, movements, stations and stories of the app, and the built
   atlas/ and texts/ folders (the Atlas core, the world's events with the conflicts, the sites, the catalogue's text records, the list of books with pictures). Checks:
   1. the date parser (relWindow): the classes of STRUCTURE_AUDIT.md C4, every Library date, hostile input; and relTies equals the Random card's psgTies for every text of the Library;
   2. for every kind, about 25 ids chosen as none / one / many links (and the ids of the audit's own examples): the groups come only from the ten labels, in that order, none empty, at most five items before “N more”, every
      address resolves against the data it names, no repeated link, the tradition's own page never among its own links; the order inside a group (parents before branches, a copy to read before one to look for, events nearest first);
      and, from the data itself, every religion an event or a conflict names exists and every one of them shows that event on its page (the inverse maps are checked against a plain scan);
   3. the box: exactly one section with one “Related” heading, no group heading without an item, five groups open and the rest under one closed “More related”, plain # addresses, no script, hostile titles escaped, nothing at all
      for a page with no groups, an unknown kind or a hostile id; and pgFoot;
   4. the words: no loaded word of the history and conflicts guards and no influence verb in anything the strip writes (group labels, tags, the notes under a heading and every small line);
   4b. the final audit of 22 November 2026 (FINAL_AUDIT.md, work package 1): a strip of one item is one quiet line and never sits under the heading (counted over every id of every kind with the options the pages pass; the event panel's
      call leaves nothing: opts.has); a picture page's strip holds none of the links the page draws (84 books); a story keeps only “On the map”, a station its religions and your marks; a calendar's “Traditions” is the religions that
      name it and one line counting the branches of them; on a phone (REL_COMPACT: 560 px) three items to a group and three groups open, the rest under the one “More related”, the same links; “filed with its texts”; the reader's
      two strips never list the same event; the stylesheet block;
   5. the pages: which page files call relatedBox( (the tradition hub is REQUIRED; the others are listed PENDING until their session lands: this test then says so, and the list is moved across by hand), the hub's one
      “Not recorded for this tradition” line instead of its empty cards, and the stylesheet block (rem, no pixel font sizes).
   Run: node tests/related.test.js */
